Hi,

This came up in a working session and nobody had the same definition.

The resilience plan lists systems, but customers experience end-to-end servic=
es that cross ATM, card, transaction and communication processes.

I do not want a dashboard that simply counts the outcome. Start with the comp=
eting explanations: manual workarounds create later reconciliation breaks; re=
covery restores authorisation before posting catches up; or cash access degra=
des before account servicing.

Several teams are reporting more failed or retried activity than they expecte=
d, but they do not agree on the cause. Different teams have produced differen=
t answers from the same period, so population and timing rules need to be vis=
ible. We looked at a version of this before. For the October 2020 review, ple=
ase show what changed and whether the earlier conclusion still holds.=20

What we need to decide is the order in which critical services should be reco=
vered and tested. Please bring a Power BI page with drill-through to a reprod=
ucible case list, including a few cases we can trace from source to conclusio=
n.

The available evidence is transaction-level timestamps, channels, amounts, st=
atuses and error context; ATM attempts, host responses, PIN attempts, blocked=
-card state and latency; customer contacts, complaints and suggestions; debit=
-order mandates, collection dates, suspensions and cancellations. Treat this =
as a historical service-impact rehearsal, not proof of infrastructure capacit=
y.

Thank you
